      "score": 92,
      "comments": 25,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50214373",
      "snippet": "Hey everyone,<p>Inspired by Herdr, I&#x27;ve built an agent multiplexer that I&#x27;ve been using as my daily driver for a few weeks now.<p>I think I improved on the concept in a few ways, focusing on the ergonomics I always wished I had:<p>I show you what the agents are up to, along with a running feed of their activity.\nThere&#x27;s also a simple shortcut (F1) to go to the next unread agent.<p>I use multiple accounts, so I&#x27;ve added unified launcher for Codex&#x2F;Claude Code&#x2F;Pi.\nTheres some careful ergonomics there: fast search and resume over sessions, inline usage tracking etc.<p>Many small quality of life improvements to the terminal experience:\n- Links can be copied with a click, so no need to drag-select over many lines\n- cmd+v just pastes images (even on SSH)\n- images have a thumbnail preview.\n- Built-in CPU&#x2F;Memory&#x2F;GPU usage tracking, broken down by workspace<",
      "links": []
